Z||000021||loafer87gt||09-11-2001||10:59 AM||||Tuesday, September 11, 2001 <P>Terroism Strikes US 06:41 AM - Turner "Bulldog" Hopkinson - In-House: Announcements<BR>Here is what we know: <P>CONFIRMED: Isreal is clearing several of it's buildings and it is expected it too has been bombed although this is unconfirmed.<BR>CONFIRMED: Another commercial liner has gone down 80 miles south of Pittsburgh.<BR>CONFIRMED: The US Air Force has confirmed their Rules of Engagement to fire upon any foreign aircraft in Washington and New York. <P>UNCONFIRMED: Three more planes have been hijacked.<BR>UNCONFIRMED: We have unconfirmed reports of a car bomb striking the State Department. It's also reported over 50,000 people work at the World Trade Center so casualty rates is expected to be large. <P><BR>CONFIRMED: <BR>NATO has been evacuated <BR>A large plane has crashed in Somerset Pennsylvania. <BR>Both World Trade Centers have now collapsed enclosing New York in a plume cloud of smoke. <BR>The hijacked plane that struck the World Trade Center was from Boston airport going to Los Angeles. It was Boeing 767. <BR>Both World Trade Centers has been struck by terrorists. <BR>The Pentagon has also been struck by terrorists. <BR>FAA has shut down all US flights for the following eight hours. <BR>1000 have been confirmed injured, there is not a accurate death count at this time but it is expected to rise into the hundreds as the reports from how many passengers were on the planes. <BR>Nearly every building has been evacuated in Washington, Boston, and Chicago Sears Tower. <BR>George Bush is currently in the air in Air Force One escorted by fighter planes.<BR>||||reg||1
