Z||000032||EdsB52||09-11-2001||11:24 AM||||I hated the fact that Bush was in office until now. I think he'll take the radical measures that Gore might not have. Don't get me wrong, I still don't like Bush and ultimately wish Gore were elected, but it's time for Bush to show us of what he's made. I hope he sends 25,000+ troops to each of the terrorist nations (Iran, Iraq, Palestine, etc) and force marshal-law upon them. I would like the troops to comb the entire country(s) and find the responsible parties and execute them. I would then like to see the governments of terrorist nations removed and replaced through elections by the people of the respective countries, while being overseen by the US forever (just don't use Florida ballots). I would hope Bush has the nads to summarily do this without checking with NATO or the rest of the world for approval. If any other countries' resist this action, we just lay a trail of bodies. I subscribe to the philosophy that you can attract more flies with honey than vinegar, but this situation warrants that philosophy be discarded. I just heard a 767 crashed somewhere. If Bush doesn't have the nads to act with radical measures, he's worthless. He's proven he can't run domestic issues worth a crap, if he gets radical here he can validate his overall worth. If he pusses out, he establishes he has zero positive leadership and is actually a detriment to our country. This has been the largest attack on the US since Pearl Harbor; we made the Japs yield to our military force for 50 years as we totally controlled them; why should we react differently now?<P>I know one thing; I wouldn't want to be a cab driver in New York of the towel-wearing variety.||||reg||1
