Z||000051||EdsB52||09-11-2001||12:38 PM||||The following are the stats from Pearl Harbor:<P><BR>Deaths: 2403; Wounded 1,178.<BR>Eighteen ships were sunk or seriously damaged including 5 battleships. <P>188 planes were destroyed and 162 were damaged.<P><BR>So yes, I would say the gross devastation will be determined to be worse today. However, like everything, you must contextualize it within contemporary times. The US population was approximately half of what it is now (guess), so that doubles the rate of impact. Not to mention the fact that Pearl Harbor was one of the gateways to a war that resulted in, if my memory serves me correctly, 1 million US deaths. So I don't think what happened today exceeds the devastation we realized in Pearl Harbor. <P>I always thought I would hate to level Arabic nations to get to the leaders, but after seeing the Palestinians celebrating in the streets, can someone define innocent bystander for me? I say level 'em. I hope Bush doesn't play with carefull diplomacy with this matter. I don't distinguish between Arabic nations very well and tend to generalize. I hope that logic isn't too ignorant, but it's the logic for which I subscribe. We need to take all of the Arabic nations over, physically and politically if we ever want to be free from terrorism. If the rest of the world doesn't like it; suck it.||||reg||1
Z||000052||grinthock||09-11-2001||12:45 PM||||I am at work and just had to post... First.<P>I havn't been able to get ahold of BanditBALZ, he is as you know on his HONEYMOON on florida, I am sure he's fine.<P>Here in Canada.<P>All borders are closed, our largest buildings in toronto have been evacuated, the TSE is closed and evac'd.  There are fighters everywhere, RCMP/OPP cars, I am here near the airport and it's NUTS, closed, military everywhere.<P><BR>It's nuts, this is unbelivable.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000053||EdsB52||09-11-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>I just hope that nucular war does not come form this.  I agree that whoever did this is going to pay....and for once i kinda agree with EDSB52.....but this could be a dervision for someting more horrible that may happen.  I never thought I would want to go to war...but if there was a draft today...i would go.  <P>My prayrers are with the victoms, their friends and family, and our country as a whole.  I hope we can get up from this and become a better place.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm with ya bro.....sign me back up. I served one term but will go back for another with a contengincy to be out after we slaughter the requisit rag-head ass. I'm moderate-left when it comes to rational diplomacy and reasonable measures, but when it's on, it's on.||||reg||1
Z||000054||Cheever3000||09-11-2001||12:57 PM||||My dad's a retired firefighter, was in the department 26 years.  I can tell you, the "brotherhood" among all of them is probably even greater than what you have seen or imagined.  They are the most sacrificial people on the planet.  The thought of hundreds of them being lost in those tall buildings (which they hate) while trying to save others, is simply numbing.  It's unthinkable.||||reg||1
Z||000055||Brandon86SE||09-11-2001||12:57 PM||||Alright, I see a lot of slamming going on here that shouldn't be.<P>I'm 19, and jumped out of bed this morning when my roommate told me that a plane just hit the world trade center.  I then watched the coverage for two and a half hours, skipping school.  This is by far the biggest tragedy I've seen in my lifetime.  The towers, the pentagon, and a jet downed in Penn. (my guess with that is the pilot took it down under gunpoint so it wouldn't get to any major centre)  I've been glued to the TV, and horrified with what I've seen this morning.  I feel sick to my stomach, all those people.  One of my best friend's sister works as an intern at the UN there.  I haven't yet been able to get a hold of her, to hear if she's heard from her sister or not.<P>However, I can't agree with the slamming of arabs and arabic nations taking place.  Albeit, the most likely culprit of this is Bin Laden.  However, he has released a statement denying any involvement.  I saw Arafat on TV nearly in tears commenting on the situation.  I haven't seen anything yet, but I'm sure king Hussein of Jordan (a middle eastern country) will release something very soon.  They've always kept very close ties with the US and Canada.  I can understand the emotional aspect going through everybody right now, and seeing *some*, keyword, *some* palestinians rejoicing in the streets certainly adds to it.  But there is no saying where the terrorist leaders are, and running a violent operation in the middle east will likely do nothing more than take innocent lives.  I know this will be investigated thoroughly by the FBI, CIA, etc.  Running in and scaring everyone important out of the area is not a reasonable course of action.  Stealth, and a quiet operation is the only way to really find the people involved.<P>Saying all arabs are terrorists, and that the whole middle east should be taken over and controlled by the US is wrong, immoral, and bordering racist.  Please nobody take this as overly offensive, as I understand the state of heightened emotions everyone is going through right now.<P>My prayers go out to everyone involved in the situation.<P>Brandon||||reg||8
